data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** The syntax is straightforward:

```csharp
Span<nint> signedSpan = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsignedSpan = stackalloc nuint[4];
```

Both work in a safe context without any special flags. On this 64-bit system each element is 8 bytes (they'd be 4 bytes on a 32-bit runtime). The only gotcha is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context — use `nint.Size` instead.
